                    briefing_text_r1:       `The Q1 tracker shows the first satisfaction decline in eight years: <strong>78% → 69%</strong>, brand equity 64 → 58, and the SERVQUAL service-quality gap at <strong>1.8 points</strong>, its worst ever. Don’t treat the symptom. Decompose the gap, locate its <em>source</em>, and decide what is the symptom and what is the cause — per Kang’s chain from internal service to customer outcomes. Your diagnostic already shows tellers waiting <strong>4.2 days for IT</strong> and <strong>6 days for credit</strong> against a 1-day standard, while front-line engagement has fallen to 61%. Size the cost of inaction: ~190,000 customers/year at <em>₱410M per attrition point</em>.`,
